  "premise_review": [
    "Preserve C : Type u, Category.{v} C, universe w and all dependent Cover C U / S.Index / S.localObject i types exactly.",
    "IsCover is a supplied predicate on the original finite-family Cover carrier. PullbackData S f is an arbitrary supplied Type w, and the record has no ∀ S f, Nonempty(PullbackData S f) premise or construction.",
    "pullbackCover takes explicit S, f : V ⟶ U and p : PullbackData S f. The source states no commutative square, universal property, or compatibility equation between the output arrows and f.",
    "transitiveComposite takes S and each family at its member object. Its precise flattening/index/arrow behavior is not axiomatized; the source only supplies the operation and its covering-law field.",
    "identityCovering requires the identity family to satisfy IsCover. pullbackStable additionally requires p and IsCover S; transitiveCovering requires IsCover S and IsCover of every member family. All conditions remain explicit.",
    "The three named theorems are exactly projections of those three supplied law fields. They do not inhabit the record, construct pullbacks, or show arbitrary finite families are covering.",
    "No concrete site, categorical pullback existence, sieve-based Grothendieck topology or sheaf/descent result is asserted by this candidate.",
    "All4 top-level commands, operation/field types, universe/category context, hypotheses and complete proof bytes are exact copies. Added open Folder.Site preserves original Cover lookup after containing-namespace rebinding; compatibility remains unreplayed."
  ],
